description:
FILED s521c (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-18) from the #1576 one-file acceptance run of Path-Tiny t/temp.t (subtest "tempfile", row "cached_temp": isa_ok sees "The class (or class-like) 'GLOB(0x1)'").

A blessed GLOB returned from a sub loses its class: `ref` answers "".

REPRO (probed, perl 5.40.3 vs PCL on 0b836815 + s521c):
    use File::Temp;
    my $t = File::Temp->new; my $h = { t => $t };
    sub ct { $_[0]->{t} }
    print ref($t), "|", ref($h->{t}), "|", ref(ct($h)), "\n";
perl: File::Temp|File::Temp|File::Temp      PCL: File::Temp|File::Temp|
REACH: Path-Tiny temp.t "cached_temp" (Path::Tiny->tempfile->cached_temp), and any accessor that returns a File::Temp / IO::Handle object.  Area: #3433 (s521a: a glob ref carries its bless class on the glob through the handle table) -- the sub-return copy path does not.
